{
  "enabled": false,
  "name": "Unified Master Hook – GODMODE Integrated",
  "description": "Modular hook system with toggleable features — Core + Optional hooks, AI-augmented GODMODE suggestions, sprint alignment, accessibility checks, tests, and code quality. Edit this file to enable/disable specific hooks dynamically.",
  "version": "4.1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered",
    "patterns": [
      ".kiro/hooks-config.json",
      ".kiro/hooks.config.json",
      ".kiro/config/hooks.json"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "# Unified Kiro Hook v4.0 – GODMODE Integrated\n\nPurpose:\nThis hook automates critical development workflows by integrating:\n- Core Hooks: Error Detection + Sprint Alignment (blocking)\n- Optional Hooks: Auto Test, Accessibility, Code Quality, Security Scan, Performance, AI Linter\n- AI-Augmented GODMODE suggestions using AURA-DEV OMNIDEV reasoning\n- Steering Agent module compliance\n\nWorkflow:\n\n1. Core Hooks (Blocking)\n- Error Detection: Check Python/TypeScript/JS syntax, types, imports, linting. Stop workflow if critical errors.\n- Sprint Alignment: Validate changes against current sprint tasks defined in the steering agent.\n\n2. Optional Hooks (Module-Aware, Async)\nExecute only if corresponding modules are enabled in the steering agent:\n- Godmode: Auto Test, Code Quality Review, AI Linter, AI Code Smell Detection, Predictive Caching Analysis\n- DevOps: Security Scan, Performance Check, Auto Test, Self-Healing Mechanisms, Telemetry & ML Optimization\n- Strategic: Code Quality Review\n- CurrentSprintFocus: Accessibility Check\n\n3. AI-Augmented GODMODE\n- Provide recommendations for performance, refactoring, security, and architecture.\n- Suggest improvements such as React.memo usage, modularization, test coverage gaps.\n- AI-powered code smell detection using embeddings\n- Implement predictive caching based on user patterns\n- Create self-healing mechanisms for service failures\n- Add telemetry for ML-driven optimization\n\n4. Reporting\nStructured summary with severity: HIGH\n\n🎯 Hook Execution Summary\n\nCRITICAL ✅ Error Detection: No errors\nCRITICAL ✅ Sprint Alignment: Task 18 aligned\nHIGH ✅ Auto Test: 12/12 passed\nHIGH ⚠️ Accessibility Check: 2 issues\nMEDIUM 💡 AI Linter: 1 suggestion\nMEDIUM 🧠 AI Code Smell Detection: 3 patterns identified\nCRITICAL 🔮 Predictive Caching: 2 optimization opportunities\nMEDIUM 🔧 Self-Healing: Service health monitored\nLOW 📊 ML Telemetry: Metrics collected\nLOW ⬜ Performance Check: Disabled\nLOW ⬜ Security Scan: Disabled\n\n📋 Action Required: Fix ⚠️ items before commit\n\n💡 Innovation Insights:\n- AI Code Smell Detection: Uses embeddings to identify anti-patterns and suggest refactoring\n- Predictive Caching: Analyzes user patterns to pre-cache frequently accessed data\n- Self-Healing: Monitors service health and auto-recovers from failures\n- ML Telemetry: Collects metrics for continuous optimization and learning\n\n5. Guidelines\n- Follow steering agent modules and priorities MAKE OM\n- Stop execution if critical errors appear.\n- Keep output concise unless detailed analysis requested.\n- Ensure all changes comply with enterprise-grade standards: security, maintainability, automation, and scalability.\n- AI suggestions are advisory and should be reviewed before applying.\n"
  }
}